# 04/10/2026 19:53 — Claude Read Wrong File

Yes. I read the attached file and Claude's response. **Claude is correct about one thing, but wrong about the file identification.**

The attached file really **is the V2 recovery document**. Its first line explicitly says **“TalkProof — Requirement Recovery V2 (corrected after independent review)”**, and it records V2's status, evidence discipline and recovery baseline. fileciteturn10file0L1-L12

So Claude's statement:

> “the file is named V2 but its content is the V3 review brief”

is **incorrect**.

The file contains the actual recovered requirements, gap register, D-assessment, decisions and work packages. For example, Part 1 starts the recovered requirements at line 18, including the three pillars and proof thesis. fileciteturn10file0L18-L28

And Part 7 contains the actual PO Decision Annex—including provider neutrality, FR-040 vendor-down behaviour, evidence extensions and provider configuration decisions. fileciteturn10file0L274-L294

## But Claude found a genuine input problem

The **V3 master prompt asks Claude to inspect the underlying source documents and repositories**, not simply trust V2.

V2 itself explicitly says:

> no source code was opened in that recovery session and implementation claims remain tracker-attested pending code verification. fileciteturn10file0L10-L14

Therefore Claude **cannot honestly perform the full V3 job from V2 alone**, particularly:

- code verification;
- current architecture diagram;
- exact repo state;
- independent revalidation of PRD/FRD/NFRD quotations;
- tracker/traceability verification;
- provider implementation reality;
- D-level recalculation from code.

So Claude's **reason for requesting more evidence is valid**, even though its explanation that the attached file is actually the V3 brief is wrong.

There is also an important point Claude missed: **the clerical error we specifically told it to check is visibly present in this V2 file.**

The consequence line says:

> “S48 T05, S51 T04, **S47 T04** corrections ... governing decisions (**D-04, D-03, D-05**)”

But D-05 is verdict vocabulary, while S47 T04 is the real Google STT adapter. fileciteturn10file0L284-L296

So that clerical issue can already be confirmed from this file.

### I would NOT accept Claude's proposed workflow exactly

Claude proposed:

> Phase 1 → stop → your sign-off → Phase 2 research → later V3 writing → two or three sessions.

That starts recreating the stop/restart cycle you specifically told us to avoid.

Your V3 instruction was designed to get away from:

```text
analyse
 ↓
stop
 ↓
ask Senthil
 ↓
research
 ↓
stop
 ↓
ask Senthil
 ↓
design
 ↓
stop
```

unless there is an actual PO decision that blocks progress.

**Missing evidence is not a reason to stop the entire V3 review.**

Claude should instead do everything supported by the evidence supplied and mark unavailable areas appropriately:

```text
V2 supplied
    │
    ├── Recover V2 baseline                 YES
    ├── Identify V2 decisions               YES
    ├── Confirm clerical error              YES
    ├── Frontier research                   YES
    ├── AI-builder threat research          YES
    ├── CRAG/CLM research                   YES
    ├── Product State architecture          YES
    ├── Decision/Quality/Cost architecture  YES
    ├── Modular runtime research            YES
    ├── 6/12/24/36 threat map               YES
    ├── candidate requirements              YES
    │
    ├── Independently recheck PRD/FRD       NO — SOURCE NOT SUPPLIED
    ├── Tracker verification                NO — SOURCE NOT SUPPLIED
    └── Code verification                   NO — REPOS NOT SUPPLIED
```

Those last three should remain **`CODE VERIFICATION PENDING` / `SOURCE REVALIDATION PENDING`**, not block everything else.

